        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-25T19:43:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For a normal suspend entry request, just the expected `PDC_CMD_SUSPEND_REQUEST_EVENT`, which the current code clears. The driver will finish its current task first before transitioning to suspend.\n\nBut the driver also uses the suspend state to disable itself in certain initialization failure scenarios, and some events (usually `PDC_CMD_EVENT`) can be left set that can\u0027t be cleared any other way once suspended. There is room for improvement on how we handle such errors that I am working on, but once we are in suspend we have to cancel everything to be safe and prevent the thread\u0027s main loop from shooting through infinitely.",
      "parentUuid": "90e239d1_9bc2379f",
